WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.890
<i>There comes a time
for every vampire...</i>

3
00:01:32.059 --> 00:01:37.327
<i>...when the idea of eternity becomes
momentarily unbearable.</i>

4
00:01:37.531 --> 00:01:41.729
<i>Living and feeding in the shadows
with only your own company...</i>

5
00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:45.929
<i>...rots into a solitary.
hollow existence.</i>

6
00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.767
<i>Immortality seems like a good idea...</i>

7
00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:53.077
<i>...until you realize
you're going to spend it alone.</i>

8
00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:57.808
<i>So I slept. hoping the sounds
of the passing eras would fade out...</i>

9
00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.247
<i>...and a sort of death might happen.</i>

10
00:02:00.454 --> 00:02:05.119
<i>But as I lay there. the world didn't
sound like the place I had left...</i>

11
00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:08.857
<i>...but something different.</i>

12
00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.523
<i>Better...</i>

13
00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:48.398
<i>It became worthwhile to rise again
as new gods were born and worshiped.</i>

14
00:02:48.602 --> 00:02:51.799
<i>Night and day. they were never alone.</i>

15
00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:55.805
<i>I would become one of them.</i>

16
00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:28.435
<i>Whether it was the meal or
the 100 years of rest. I'm not sure.</i>

17
00:03:28.642 --> 00:03:32.044
<i>But suddenly
I was feeling better than ever.</i>

18
00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:34.406
<i>My senses so high...</i>

19
00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:39.450
<i>...they led me straight to the
instrument of my resurrection...</i>

20
00:03:39.653 --> 00:03:43.590
<i>...playing in my old house.</i>

21
00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.553
Jesus.

22
00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.415
Your voice...

23
00:04:17.858 --> 00:04:19.292
Who the hell are you?

24
00:04:19.493 --> 00:04:23.930
<i>The question provoked
an irresistible urge.</i>

25
00:04:24.131 --> 00:04:27.066
I am the vampire Lestat.

26
00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:29.326
<i>It just rolled out of my mouth.</i>

27
00:04:29.536 --> 00:04:33.200
<i>With one sentence.
I betrayed everything about my kind.</i>

28
00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:35.431
<i>Betrayed our code of secrecy.</i>

29
00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:37.701
Vampire?

30
00:04:38.145 --> 00:04:41.479
-That's funny.
-Indeed.

31
00:04:41.715 --> 00:04:44.207
Hilarious.

32
00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:47.086
You're all...

33
00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.982
...so beautiful.

34
00:04:49.523 --> 00:04:53.187
-Your hands are--
-Cold as death?

35
00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.456
-You're gonna kill us?
-No.

36
00:04:56.763 --> 00:05:01.599
All that you've ever dreamed of.
I'm going to make yours.

37
00:05:01.802 --> 00:05:04.430
This is your lucky day.

38
00:05:04.638 --> 00:05:07.005
<i>It was a bold move. I admit.</i>

39
00:05:07.207 --> 00:05:11.610
<i>But from that moment on they were
my friends. my children. my band.</i>

40
00:05:11.812 --> 00:05:15.373
<i>Giving the world a new god.
Me.</i>

41
00:07:06.526 --> 00:07:12.124
Okay. can I have your attention?
Okay. some questions. One at a time.

42
00:07:13.333 --> 00:07:15.893
-Yeah. you.
-So why here in London?

43
00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:18.696
We go where we're told to. like you.

44
00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:24.207
-How would you sum up your music?
-Sex. blood and rock and roll.

45
00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:26.539
Okay. excuse me.

46
00:07:27.847 --> 00:07:29.372
It's time.

47
00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:31.243
May I present...

48
00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:35.149
...the vampire Lestat.

49
00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.289
<i>Good evening.</i>

50
00:07:42.796 --> 00:07:47.529
<i>Sorry I'm late. I was just trying
to catch my breakfast.</i>

51
00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:53.739
Okay. can we keep it short?
One at a time.

52
00:07:54.007 --> 00:07:55.202
Yeah. you.

53
00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:59.339
I may be wrong. but what
I remember about vampires is...

54
00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:02.607
...you generally keep
your identity secret.

55
00:08:02.816 --> 00:08:06.309
<i>Yes. But why hide it
in this day and age?</i>

56
00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:09.148
<i>I've hidden in the shadows
for centuries.</i>

57
00:08:09.356 --> 00:08:12.087
<i>It's time to share myself
with the world.</i>

58
00:08:12.659 --> 00:08:17.495
Could you prove it? You know. give us
a demonstration of your powers.

59
00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:22.965
<i>If you like. I can give you a private
demonstration in your hotel tonight.</i>

60
00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:31.375
Your first and only concert's
in Death Valley. just days away.

61
00:08:31.578 --> 00:08:35.037
-Why just the one?
<i>-I don't like repeating myself.</i>

62
00:08:35.248 --> 00:08:40.118
There are rumors about
the hidden meaning in your lyrics...

63
00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:44.018
...that you're giving away
vampire secrets. Is that true?

64
00:08:44.224 --> 00:08:49.663
<i>Maybe I'm trying to resurrect a few
old friends. Daring them to come out.</i>

65
00:08:49.863 --> 00:08:54.300
Won't these vampires be pissed off
that you're giving away secrets?

66
00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:58.302
<i>I imagine they are. yes.</i>

67
00:08:58.505 --> 00:09:02.100
Do you have anything to say
to the other vampires?

68
00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:05.369
<i>As a matter of fact. I do.</i>

69
00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:11.713
<i>Come out. come out. wherever you are.</i>

70
00:09:13.486 --> 00:09:17.116
<i>See you all in Death Valley.</i>

71
00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:43.978
I heard Lestat keeps all these girls
in his cellar. And it's nice.

72
00:09:44.184 --> 00:09:46.846
They give you food
and cable and weed.

73
00:09:47.053 --> 00:09:48.543
Oh. please.

74
00:09:48.755 --> 00:09:53.556
But you have to let him suck you
on your neck whenever he wants.

75
00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.923
-Doesn't sound too bad.
-Done worse.

76
00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:59.030
-I'll say.
-This way. girls.

77
00:10:12.579 --> 00:10:15.207
So this is Lestat's house?

78
00:10:15.415 --> 00:10:18.749
It is this week. We move around a lot.

79
00:10:18.952 --> 00:10:20.442
Why is that?

80
00:10:21.154 --> 00:10:24.385
What can I say? The guy is just...

81
00:10:25.992 --> 00:10:31.487
-Boss. I didn't see you there.
-No. You wouldn't. would you?

82
00:10:35.068 --> 00:10:38.504
These are the girls
that you asked for.

83
00:10:39.205 --> 00:10:40.764
Yes.

84
00:10:56.456 --> 00:10:59.619
Do you want me to take
the girls home later?

85
00:10:59.826 --> 00:11:01.988
No. thank you. Roger.

86
00:11:02.195 --> 00:11:04.857
I'll make sure they're taken care of.

87
00:11:07.634 --> 00:11:09.659
You want some?

88
00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:12.661
Want me?

89
00:11:13.673 --> 00:11:15.402
You hungry?

90
00:11:19.646 --> 00:11:23.173
You hungry for something else?

91
00:11:27.353 --> 00:11:29.082
Come on.

92
00:11:29.589 --> 00:11:33.048
-Don't you want to have some fun?
-Don't do that.

93
00:11:33.393 --> 00:11:35.760
Are you ticklish?

94
00:11:35.962 --> 00:11:38.624
I'm very ticklish.

95
00:12:44.697 --> 00:12:46.859
Come out. come out...

96
00:12:47.066 --> 00:12:49.501
...whoever you are.

97
00:12:57.677 --> 00:12:59.441
<i>Jesse.</i>

98
00:13:01.281 --> 00:13:04.444
<i>Jesse.</i>

99
00:13:04.651 --> 00:13:06.210
<i>A voice...</i>

100
00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.282
<i>...calling to me...</i>

101
00:13:09.489 --> 00:13:11.583
<i>...in my dreams.</i>

102
00:13:11.791 --> 00:13:15.455
<i>The same dream I've had
since I was 6.</i>

103
00:13:15.862 --> 00:13:18.729
<i>I have a family of my own.</i>

104
00:13:19.032 --> 00:13:21.694
<i>Not a strange dream. really.</i>

105
00:13:21.901 --> 00:13:24.632
<i>One every orphan has.</i>

106
00:13:52.398 --> 00:13:54.264
I'm sorry. but you must go.

107
00:13:54.467 --> 00:13:58.267
Why can't I stay with you?
Please. Aunt Maharet.

108
00:13:58.471 --> 00:14:01.930
I don't want you to go. But you must.

109
00:14:02.375 --> 00:14:05.208
Aunt. you're bleeding.

110
00:14:11.918 --> 00:14:13.943
You must be with your own.

111
00:14:14.153 --> 00:14:18.818
<i>-I knew things were not normal.
-This isn't the life I wanted for you.</i>

112
00:14:19.025 --> 00:14:23.121
<i>I only knew I was part of them.
and being cast out...</i>

113
00:14:23.329 --> 00:14:24.626
<i>Was I bad?</i>

114
00:14:24.831 --> 00:14:26.925
<i>Had I done something wrong?</i>

115
00:14:27.133 --> 00:14:29.625
I'll always be watching over you.

116
00:14:29.836 --> 00:14:32.305
I want to stay with you forever.

117
00:14:32.505 --> 00:14:35.031
You can't.

118
00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:13.006
<i>I'm Serena Altschul. MTV News.</i>

119
00:15:13.212 --> 00:15:18.150
<i>Vampire turned rocker Lestat
has returned with a new CD.</i> Forsaken.

120
00:15:18.351 --> 00:15:20.342
<i>Although from New Orleans...</i>

121
00:15:20.553 --> 00:15:24.148
<i>...he claims to be an 18th-century
French nobleman...</i>

122
00:15:24.323 --> 00:15:27.020
<i>...who has been asleep
for over 100 years.</i>

123
00:15:27.226 --> 00:15:32.995
<i>Here's a look at the new video
from the debut album. "Redeemer."</i>

124
00:16:41.701 --> 00:16:44.500
<i>Like everyone. I assumed
Lestat was a joke.</i>

125
00:16:44.704 --> 00:16:49.835
A rock star with a gimmick. Then one
of his lyrics caught my attention.

126
00:16:50.176 --> 00:16:53.407
"Take a walk down the aisle
at the end of the mile.

127
00:16:53.579 --> 00:16:56.913
Give your life to my charms
in the Admiral's Arms."

128
00:16:57.116 --> 00:16:58.641
That rang a bell.

129
00:16:58.851 --> 00:17:01.479
I tracked down old leases in London.

130
00:17:01.687 --> 00:17:05.851
It turns out in the late 1600s
there was a pub in Mile End...

131
00:17:06.025 --> 00:17:07.925
...called the Admiral's Arms.

132
00:17:08.127 --> 00:17:11.324
It had a reputation for dealing
with black magic...

133
00:17:11.531 --> 00:17:14.091
...and reports of people vanishing.

134
00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:19.636
Here's where you could find
the Admiral's Arms in old London.

135
00:17:19.839 --> 00:17:22.831
That part of London
is mostly warehouses...

136
00:17:23.042 --> 00:17:27.172
...meat-packing plants and
a private club in the same location.

137
00:17:28.481 --> 00:17:31.917
I think that it's a vampire coven.

138
00:17:32.118 --> 00:17:34.917
And Lestat is leading us to it.

139
00:17:36.989 --> 00:17:40.084
-Who took this picture?
-I did.

140
00:17:40.293 --> 00:17:44.025
You're still an apprentice.
You don't do field work.

141
00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:45.857
The Talamasca has a code.

142
00:17:46.065 --> 00:17:49.695
I know. "Observe the dark realm.
but be not of it."

143
00:17:49.902 --> 00:17:52.837
Well. it's held good for 12 centuries.

144
00:17:53.039 --> 00:17:56.976
We record and observe.
but never interfere.

145
00:17:57.176 --> 00:17:59.270
I had to see it for myself.

146
00:18:02.181 --> 00:18:04.377
Is David aware of this?

147
00:18:04.917 --> 00:18:05.941
Jesse?

148
00:18:08.521 --> 00:18:09.511
Hello. David.

149
00:18:10.289 --> 00:18:14.021
-I was explaining--
-Why don't you see me in my office?

150
00:18:17.263 --> 00:18:20.426
This is a real coven.
In the middle of London.

151
00:18:20.633 --> 00:18:23.967
All the more reason
to have told me first.

152
00:18:25.638 --> 00:18:27.265
Listen. Jesse...

153
00:18:30.743 --> 00:18:33.303
...we know about Lestat.

154
00:18:33.779 --> 00:18:36.510
What he's doing is unprecedented.

155
00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.143
So why is he doing it?

156
00:18:39.352 --> 00:18:42.947
Aren't you curious?
Don't you think we should find out?

157
00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:46.518
Let me show you something.

158
00:18:49.629 --> 00:18:51.529
What do you see?

159
00:18:54.233 --> 00:18:56.895
Mid-1500s. Florence.

160
00:18:58.004 --> 00:18:59.563
This one?

161
00:19:03.376 --> 00:19:06.437
-This man is in both.
-Yes.

162
00:19:08.781 --> 00:19:11.148
All the different paint samples...

163
00:19:11.817 --> 00:19:13.717
...all authentic.

164
00:19:13.919 --> 00:19:17.549
Each painted at the time
of their particular style.

165
00:19:24.163 --> 00:19:26.325
His name is Marius.

166
00:19:27.199 --> 00:19:30.032
I've been tracing him for years.

167
00:19:30.503 --> 00:19:32.597
My little obsession.

168
00:19:32.805 --> 00:19:35.934
The closest we've come
to the original vampire.

169
00:19:36.208 --> 00:19:39.872
Marius himself dates back to 400 B.C.

170
00:19:43.215 --> 00:19:45.741
So he's older than Lestat.

171
00:19:45.951 --> 00:19:48.113
He made Lestat.

172
00:19:48.821 --> 00:19:50.186
How do you know that?

173
00:19:50.389 --> 00:19:53.256
Because I have Lestat's journal.

174
00:19:56.662 --> 00:19:58.130
I want to see it.

175
00:20:00.466 --> 00:20:03.527
Promise me you'll never
go back to that place.

176
00:20:34.867 --> 00:20:38.326
<i>It was the winter of 1788.</i>

177
00:20:38.537 --> 00:20:43.498
<i>And I was brought to a Mediterranean
island by the man who made me.</i>

178
00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:48.542
<i>If a man is what you'd call him.</i>

179
00:21:38.063 --> 00:21:40.430
Lestat. welcome.

180
00:21:42.535 --> 00:21:43.969
Who are you?

181
00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:46.104
Do I know you?

182
00:21:48.641 --> 00:21:52.544
I am unknowable by nature.
but you may call me Marius.

183
00:21:52.745 --> 00:21:57.546
I'm the lord of a great manor.
They'll send an army to look for me.

184
00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:00.776
I doubt they'll find you.
Lord de Lioncourt.

185
00:22:00.986 --> 00:22:02.977
You're a long way from home.

186
00:22:32.218 --> 00:22:33.845
You're weak...

187
00:22:34.353 --> 00:22:35.821
...near passing.

188
00:22:37.623 --> 00:22:40.251
I can barely hear your heartbeat.

189
00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:46.662
The future hastens.
An age beyond my antique reason.

190
00:22:46.866 --> 00:22:49.836
You will help me understand
these times.

191
00:22:50.236 --> 00:22:52.330
That's why I chose you.

192
00:22:52.705 --> 00:22:54.230
Chose me for what?

193
00:23:04.149 --> 00:23:05.548
Drink...

194
00:23:06.085 --> 00:23:07.678
...and live.

195
00:23:08.654 --> 00:23:11.885
You've been brave enough
for one night. my son.

196
00:23:14.627 --> 00:23:16.789
Drink...

197
00:23:18.297 --> 00:23:20.288
...and learn.

198
00:23:22.668 --> 00:23:25.262
Good. is it not?

199
00:23:29.074 --> 00:23:31.600
No more. No more. Lestat.

200
00:23:33.078 --> 00:23:34.944
No more!

201
00:24:09.281 --> 00:24:11.682
Don't be afraid.

202
00:24:11.951 --> 00:24:14.977
It's only your body that dies.

203
00:24:29.468 --> 00:24:31.800
More.

204
00:24:34.139 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>I impressed my maker
with my thirst for things.</i>

205
00:24:37.910 --> 00:24:40.538
<i>He set out to educate me
in the unknown.</i>

206
00:24:40.713 --> 00:24:45.344
<i>Taught me all about the world.
its hidden history...</i>

207
00:24:45.551 --> 00:24:47.952
<i>...and about myself.</i>

208
00:24:53.425 --> 00:24:55.757
That's enough. my son.

209
00:24:58.630 --> 00:25:01.895
When you feed. hold back
from the moment of death.

210
00:25:02.101 --> 00:25:06.663
Never take the last drop. or it will
draw you in and you will die.

211
00:25:12.111 --> 00:25:14.409
Appreciate your prey.

212
00:25:19.551 --> 00:25:23.852
Their blood that we take into us
carries with it life...

213
00:25:24.056 --> 00:25:28.721
...their life. their knowledge.
their complexity.

214
00:25:31.764 --> 00:25:35.325
<i>My senses run amuck.
like a newborn child.</i>

215
00:25:36.168 --> 00:25:41.572
<i>And as for my new powers. I was beside
myself with the pleasure of it all.</i>

216
00:25:44.076 --> 00:25:45.737
We've stayed long enough.

217
00:25:45.944 --> 00:25:47.742
But we've spoken to no one.

218
00:25:48.313 --> 00:25:51.078
A vampire's life
is a life of discretion.

219
00:25:51.283 --> 00:25:52.876
Discretion?

220
00:25:53.552 --> 00:25:55.520
Why must we hide. Marius?

221
00:25:55.721 --> 00:25:59.055
We are the powerful.
we are the immortal.

222
00:25:59.258 --> 00:26:02.751
We should walk fearless
in the open. no?

223
00:26:13.472 --> 00:26:15.736
That cannot be.

224
00:26:16.742 --> 00:26:19.439
We're vulnerable during the day.

225
00:26:19.645 --> 00:26:23.775
Mortals must never know about us.
for the sake of all our kind.

226
00:26:24.283 --> 00:26:26.445
So I could never know her?

227
00:26:26.652 --> 00:26:28.984
Not unless you wanted to kill her.

228
00:26:36.295 --> 00:26:38.127
So I can never be known?

229
00:26:40.799 --> 00:26:43.598
You must be dead to the world.

230
00:26:44.803 --> 00:26:47.170
Come on. time to leave.

231
00:27:48.167 --> 00:27:50.431
Sophia. run! Run!

232
00:27:50.769 --> 00:27:53.136
Go! Go--

233
00:27:53.972 --> 00:27:55.235
Lestat...

234
00:27:55.440 --> 00:27:57.738
...stop her!

235
00:27:58.510 --> 00:27:59.568
You must!

236
00:28:37.182 --> 00:28:41.085
We must remain in the shadows.

237
00:28:42.521 --> 00:28:46.082
You still have a few
lingering mortal emotions.

238
00:28:47.192 --> 00:28:50.526
They'll serve you no good. my friend.

239
00:29:03.108 --> 00:29:05.042
Forgive me.

240
00:29:12.084 --> 00:29:18.148
<i>The faces of my victims haunted me.
reminding me of my fate.</i>

241
00:29:18.357 --> 00:29:20.724
<i>For nights and days I played...</i>

242
00:29:20.926 --> 00:29:26.660
<i>...furious that I would never partake
of the simple joys of the world.</i>

243
00:29:26.865 --> 00:29:29.061
<i>I was meant for more than this.</i>

244
00:30:08.674 --> 00:30:10.574
Marius?

245
00:31:31.990 --> 00:31:34.618
Would you like me to play for you?

246
00:34:02.641 --> 00:34:05.235
What have you done. Lestat?

247
00:34:14.553 --> 00:34:18.251
-More!
-I don't think so. my little lord.

248
00:34:18.490 --> 00:34:20.515
-Let me go.
-No.

249
00:34:20.725 --> 00:34:24.184
You've had the purest blood.
seen the oldest things.

250
00:34:24.396 --> 00:34:29.857
-Far too much for one as young as you.
-Her blood is like liquid fire.

251
00:34:30.068 --> 00:34:31.467
Who is she?

252
00:34:36.908 --> 00:34:39.036
She's your mother.

253
00:34:39.244 --> 00:34:41.303
She's my mother.

254
00:34:41.513 --> 00:34:45.677
Akasha. the queen of all
who are damned.

255
00:34:46.318 --> 00:34:48.252
And he's her king.

256
00:34:48.753 --> 00:34:53.953
Akasha and Enkil nearly drank this
earth dry when they ruled over Egypt.

257
00:34:54.125 --> 00:34:58.119
They drank until Enkil
lost his will to drink.

258
00:34:58.296 --> 00:35:03.257
Without her mate beside her. she also
lost hers. They became living statues.

259
00:35:03.435 --> 00:35:09.067
She respects nothing except the taste
of blood. human and immortal alike.

260
00:35:09.441 --> 00:35:10.966
No. Release me!

261
00:35:17.048 --> 00:35:19.449
She made you quite powerful.

262
00:35:19.618 --> 00:35:21.848
You'll not stop me!

263
00:35:23.121 --> 00:35:25.988
Can I hear her blood in your voice?

264
00:35:26.791 --> 00:35:30.318
In all the years of my care.
not once have they moved.

265
00:35:30.528 --> 00:35:34.226
Until tonight. And she chose me.

266
00:35:35.133 --> 00:35:36.760
I chose you.

267
00:35:40.805 --> 00:35:44.139
Where are you going?! Marius!

268
00:36:41.566 --> 00:36:47.903
<i>Many times since. I have called
to Marius. But there was no answer.</i>

269
00:36:48.440 --> 00:36:52.934
<i>Just the endless procession
of days. months...</i>

270
00:36:53.111 --> 00:36:54.636
<i>...years.</i>

271
00:36:55.814 --> 00:36:59.478
<i>My teacher left me
to my darkest lesson.</i>

272
00:36:59.651 --> 00:37:01.813
<i>That in the end. we are alone.</i>

273
00:37:02.721 --> 00:37:08.683
<i>And there is nothing but the cold.
dark wasteland of eternity.</i>

274
00:37:33.585 --> 00:37:37.044
<i>David thought the journal
would satisfy my curiosity.</i>

275
00:37:37.722 --> 00:37:40.919
<i>But it only made me want
to know more.</i>

276
00:37:41.092 --> 00:37:43.789
<i>I had to go back
to the Admiral's Arms.</i>

277
00:37:43.962 --> 00:37:46.397
<i>I had no choice.</i>

278
00:38:22.901 --> 00:38:25.893
<i>This is a fantastic place. I love it.</i>

279
00:38:26.571 --> 00:38:29.336
You sure I can't get you a drink?

280
00:38:30.308 --> 00:38:31.605
Soon.

281
00:39:34.272 --> 00:39:35.831
Hi.

282
00:39:36.708 --> 00:39:38.107
-Hi.
-Come here often?

283
00:39:38.543 --> 00:39:40.307
All the time.

284
00:39:44.148 --> 00:39:47.015
I don't see any marks.

285
00:39:47.185 --> 00:39:49.711
You haven't seen the rest of my body.

286
00:39:50.722 --> 00:39:53.350
Is that an invitation?

287
00:39:53.524 --> 00:39:55.618
Sorry. I'm taken.

288
00:39:55.827 --> 00:39:57.625
And...

289
00:39:58.329 --> 00:40:00.388
...where is your host?

290
00:40:00.798 --> 00:40:02.163
He's here somewhere.

291
00:40:05.870 --> 00:40:09.465
This host. what's his name?

292
00:40:13.511 --> 00:40:14.808
Marius.

293
00:40:15.713 --> 00:40:18.444
Sorry. don't know the guy.

294
00:40:18.616 --> 00:40:23.053
-Of course not. He's an ancient.
-There aren't any ancients left.

295
00:40:23.221 --> 00:40:25.883
They all turned to dust.

296
00:40:26.224 --> 00:40:29.455
So unless you've got him in a bottle
somewhere...

297
00:40:29.627 --> 00:40:32.722
You're brave to joke.
I wish you could meet him.

298
00:40:32.897 --> 00:40:36.492
-And why is that?
-Because you might learn something.

299
00:40:39.971 --> 00:40:41.962
Excuse me.

300
00:40:56.354 --> 00:40:58.049
Going somewhere?

301
00:40:59.958 --> 00:41:02.928
Now this will only hurt a little bit.

302
00:41:03.328 --> 00:41:07.162
In fact. you might even enjoy it.

303
00:41:07.365 --> 00:41:08.389
Don't do this.

304
00:41:29.020 --> 00:41:30.510
Boo.

305
00:41:46.070 --> 00:41:49.438
That was quite a performance.

306
00:41:50.074 --> 00:41:52.839
You should be more careful.

307
00:41:53.978 --> 00:41:57.278
-Thanks.
-For what?

308
00:41:57.615 --> 00:41:59.447
You saved me.

309
00:42:00.118 --> 00:42:02.109
How presumptuous.

310
00:42:03.021 --> 00:42:06.548
So you know Marius?

311
00:42:08.826 --> 00:42:10.487
I know a lot of things.

312
00:42:10.695 --> 00:42:13.357
Not how to stay alive. apparently.

313
00:42:13.698 --> 00:42:15.860
I guess we have that in common.

314
00:42:16.401 --> 00:42:19.336
Although I'm a little ahead
of the race here.

315
00:42:19.537 --> 00:42:22.063
Well. I can fix that.

316
00:42:22.707 --> 00:42:27.042
Your song "Redeemer" is about
the girl with the violin. isn't it?

317
00:42:28.746 --> 00:42:29.907
Yeah.

318
00:42:30.148 --> 00:42:31.547
Is it?

319
00:42:34.519 --> 00:42:36.783
What else do you think you know?

320
00:42:37.889 --> 00:42:39.152
I...

321
00:42:39.357 --> 00:42:41.826
You're shaking.

322
00:42:42.026 --> 00:42:43.425
Cold.

323
00:42:44.429 --> 00:42:45.988
Still cold?

324
00:42:47.565 --> 00:42:51.502
Go on. Tell me more about me.

325
00:42:51.736 --> 00:42:53.363
You want...

326
00:42:53.571 --> 00:42:55.505
What do I want?

327
00:42:56.908 --> 00:43:00.344
-You yearn.
-What do I yearn?

328
00:43:03.714 --> 00:43:06.479
For what do I yearn?

329
00:43:06.651 --> 00:43:08.779
To walk with the living.

330
00:43:10.388 --> 00:43:14.848
Out of the cold.
dark wasteland of eternity.

331
00:43:18.362 --> 00:43:19.420
Well...

332
00:43:21.866 --> 00:43:25.200
...that makes you
a very clever librarian.

333
00:43:25.369 --> 00:43:27.929
Talamasca.

334
00:43:28.106 --> 00:43:31.599
I knew I left that journal somewhere.

335
00:43:34.445 --> 00:43:38.313
-Was it a good read?
-It touched me.

336
00:43:38.916 --> 00:43:40.577
Did it. now?

337
00:43:42.019 --> 00:43:43.885
Don't worry. Jesse.

338
00:43:44.322 --> 00:43:46.916
Your kind never satisfies my thirst.

339
00:43:49.927 --> 00:43:53.295
Lestat. I know something
that's not in your journal.

340
00:43:55.867 --> 00:43:56.857
What?

341
00:43:57.401 --> 00:43:59.836
You still have the violin. don't you?

342
00:44:00.505 --> 00:44:02.564
No. I understand.

343
00:44:03.508 --> 00:44:05.272
After all. it's only human.

344
00:45:01.966 --> 00:45:03.957
Clever librarian.

345
00:45:14.178 --> 00:45:18.046
David. listen. I'm going
to Los Angeles for the concert.

346
00:45:18.749 --> 00:45:21.810
<i>I met him. David. I talked to Lestat.</i>

347
00:45:22.086 --> 00:45:24.282
What? Jesse?

348
00:45:24.488 --> 00:45:28.049
Listen to me very carefully now.

349
00:45:29.694 --> 00:45:32.664
You are no longer seeing
things clearly.

350
00:45:32.830 --> 00:45:36.596
<i>Lestat told the world that vampires
live among us. They're mad.</i>

351
00:45:36.767 --> 00:45:41.329
<i>They'll be at the concert to kill him.
You've become obsessed with it.</i>

352
00:45:41.505 --> 00:45:46.238
<i>-I'm worried about you.</i>
-Don't worry about me. I'll be okay.

353
00:45:46.444 --> 00:45:48.344
I'll check in and...

354
00:45:49.413 --> 00:45:51.040
I'm sorry. I have to go.

355
00:45:51.249 --> 00:45:52.842
No. Jesse--

356
00:46:09.667 --> 00:46:13.661
<i>The city of Lost Angels already
fed on the blood of youth.</i>

357
00:46:13.838 --> 00:46:17.103
<i>My presence here barely
stirred a ripple.</i>

358
00:46:17.275 --> 00:46:19.676
<i>We had three days till the concert.</i>

359
00:46:19.877 --> 00:46:22.403
<i>I could feel something was coming.</i>

360
00:46:22.580 --> 00:46:25.743
<i>I just couldn't figure out what.</i>

361
00:46:58.582 --> 00:47:00.107
Marius.

362
00:47:12.163 --> 00:47:13.927
Lestat.

363
00:47:15.299 --> 00:47:17.768
It is good to see you. Lestat.

364
00:47:19.070 --> 00:47:20.435
And you.

365
00:47:20.671 --> 00:47:24.301
Still wearing the old fashions. I see.

366
00:47:26.110 --> 00:47:28.272
Old habits die hard.

367
00:47:28.479 --> 00:47:33.610
How did you manage to slip
through the '50s in red velvet?

368
00:47:34.318 --> 00:47:35.786
I slept.

369
00:47:37.154 --> 00:47:39.418
Don't think you missed much.

370
00:47:40.624 --> 00:47:44.322
-Elvis.
-Elvis. yes.

371
00:47:46.530 --> 00:47:48.555
You're bigger than he is now.

372
00:47:48.966 --> 00:47:49.990
So...

373
00:47:50.868 --> 00:47:52.996
After all this time...

374
00:47:53.537 --> 00:47:55.471
...what's the occasion?

375
00:47:55.639 --> 00:48:01.169
You've just become very hard to avoid
these days. at least in conversation.

376
00:48:02.179 --> 00:48:05.706
-What are you trying to prove. Lestat?
-Oh. please.

377
00:48:05.883 --> 00:48:10.116
It's a little too late to come over
all paternal now. Marius.

378
00:48:10.321 --> 00:48:14.087
Two hundred years
and not a word from you.

379
00:48:15.326 --> 00:48:18.421
You almost cost me everything.

380
00:48:21.365 --> 00:48:22.992
Now you've done it again.

381
00:48:23.601 --> 00:48:27.162
This isn't the time to settle
old scores.

382
00:48:28.806 --> 00:48:31.867
Vampires don't settle old scores.

383
00:48:33.978 --> 00:48:36.413
We harbor them.

384
00:48:40.718 --> 00:48:42.482
How did you find me?

385
00:48:43.053 --> 00:48:44.418
I made you.

386
00:48:44.755 --> 00:48:47.087
I've always known where you are.

387
00:48:47.892 --> 00:48:49.360
Besides...

388
00:48:49.693 --> 00:48:53.960
...I just had to look for the most
gauche house on the block.

389
00:48:55.633 --> 00:48:59.501
Come. Let me show you what it means
to live in the light.

390
00:49:09.413 --> 00:49:10.710
Impressive.

391
00:49:10.881 --> 00:49:15.284
Reminds me of old mad druids
running around chanting in the forest.

392
00:49:15.486 --> 00:49:17.580
A return to the primitive.

393
00:49:18.222 --> 00:49:20.247
Out there. my fans...

394
00:49:21.559 --> 00:49:23.118
...they worship me.

395
00:49:23.561 --> 00:49:28.658
Millions of arms reach out to embrace.
beg me to come into their lives.

396
00:49:28.833 --> 00:49:30.858
It's what you always wanted.

397
00:49:31.068 --> 00:49:33.730
With all my black little heart.

398
00:49:35.072 --> 00:49:38.406
Did you think of anyone but yourself?

399
00:49:38.809 --> 00:49:42.074
I only have myself.
You taught me that.

400
00:49:42.813 --> 00:49:46.215
It may be time to get ready
for some company.

401
00:49:46.383 --> 00:49:52.015
-What's that supposed to mean?
-Your music's woken an old friend.

402
00:49:54.024 --> 00:49:55.651
Can't you hear it?

403
00:49:56.160 --> 00:49:59.721
Or is the applause all you
can hear now?

404
00:50:18.849 --> 00:50:20.180
Akasha.

405
00:50:20.985 --> 00:50:22.578
Arisen.

406
00:50:23.287 --> 00:50:26.052
She has taken the king's blood.

407
00:50:26.323 --> 00:50:28.223
Absorbed his power.

408
00:50:28.859 --> 00:50:31.954
Good. Let her come.

409
00:50:32.296 --> 00:50:34.424
Cancel the concert.

410
00:50:34.732 --> 00:50:36.063
Never.

411
00:50:36.667 --> 00:50:40.626
You're no match for her. Lestat.
You're not a god.

412
00:50:41.305 --> 00:50:44.104
We were once mortals too.

413
00:50:45.142 --> 00:50:47.975
It is our heritage we protect.

414
00:50:48.145 --> 00:50:50.944
Such reverence for mortals.

415
00:50:51.148 --> 00:50:54.083
Then you should have left me as one.

416
00:51:54.812 --> 00:52:00.148
Scent is fading.
He was here too long ago.

417
00:52:00.351 --> 00:52:02.080
You like him. do you?

418
00:52:03.220 --> 00:52:05.245
He reminds me of someone.

419
00:52:05.456 --> 00:52:10.121
All he's going to remind you of soon
is a pile of bones.

420
00:52:10.394 --> 00:52:13.523
We're going to dismember him.
Bleed him dry.

421
00:52:13.697 --> 00:52:14.892
Really?

422
00:52:16.133 --> 00:52:19.569
Is that what you're going to do?

423
00:55:17.915 --> 00:55:21.374
<i>Old gods on new streets.</i>

424
00:55:21.885 --> 00:55:25.378
<i>Not only had the concert sold out
among the living...</i>

425
00:55:25.556 --> 00:55:28.685
<i>...it seemed all the undead
were coming too.</i>

426
00:55:28.892 --> 00:55:31.793
<i>There would be angry vampires
out there...</i>

427
00:55:31.962 --> 00:55:36.126
<i>...frightened of the light I was
directing on all our kind.</i>

428
00:55:36.333 --> 00:55:39.894
<i>Do you have anything to say
to the other vampires?</i>

429
00:55:40.103 --> 00:55:43.937
<i>Yes. as a matter of fact. I do.</i>

430
00:55:44.842 --> 00:55:48.278
<i>Come out. come out. wherever you are.</i>

431
00:55:49.012 --> 00:55:51.106
<i>They wanted me dead.</i>

432
00:55:51.315 --> 00:55:52.976
<i>Let them try.</i>

433
00:55:53.350 --> 00:55:54.818
<i>Bring it on.</i>

434
00:55:55.219 --> 00:55:58.018
<i>Better dead than alone.</i>

435
00:56:13.704 --> 00:56:16.230
Hey. honey. Want tickets for tomorrow?

436
00:56:16.406 --> 00:56:18.238
-Going to the show?
-No.

437
00:56:18.408 --> 00:56:22.174
-Come on. I got them for $200.
-$200?! I don't think so.

438
00:56:22.346 --> 00:56:28.251
-What if I say 150?
- 150? You're gonna cut me a deal?

439
00:56:28.452 --> 00:56:32.650
So. listen. just two girls. okay?
So how old are you again?

440
00:56:35.626 --> 00:56:38.891
-Check it out. Champagne?
-Yeah.

441
00:56:56.079 --> 00:57:01.176
Oh. my God. I can't believe
it's really you! I'm your biggest fan.

442
00:57:03.220 --> 00:57:04.619
Boo.

443
00:57:05.589 --> 00:57:06.886
Boo back.

444
00:57:07.791 --> 00:57:10.419
Lestat. I came all the way
from Tarzana.

445
00:57:10.594 --> 00:57:11.720
Really?

446
00:57:12.729 --> 00:57:14.322
-And you?
-London.

447
00:57:15.599 --> 00:57:18.193
A London Goth. I see.

448
00:57:19.303 --> 00:57:24.002
It's funny. I would have pegged you
for a Talamascan.

449
00:57:24.942 --> 00:57:26.876
Maybe in another life.

450
00:57:27.044 --> 00:57:28.671
I'm an Episcopalian.

451
00:57:29.146 --> 00:57:32.673
And I'm a frigging Buddhist.
Lestat...

452
00:57:32.849 --> 00:57:37.184
Roger. would you take our little
Episcopalian back to church?

453
00:57:37.354 --> 00:57:39.914
Just the one tonight? Sure.

454
00:57:40.123 --> 00:57:43.388
-Sweetheart. come on.
-What?

455
00:57:44.061 --> 00:57:45.688
-Come on.
-What?!

456
00:57:45.862 --> 00:57:49.059
-It's a good thing.
-Can I still go backstage?

457
00:57:50.801 --> 00:57:53.361
Why are you following me?

458
00:57:53.637 --> 00:57:55.036
What do you want?

459
00:58:08.518 --> 00:58:12.853
So you come all this way
just to return this to me?

460
00:58:13.056 --> 00:58:16.026
Out of the goodness of your heart?

461
00:58:18.695 --> 00:58:21.357
I want you to show me what it's like.

462
00:58:21.765 --> 00:58:24.894
What what is like. exactly?

463
00:58:25.068 --> 00:58:27.230
To be like you.

464
00:58:30.273 --> 00:58:32.367
I don't have time for this.

465
00:58:32.776 --> 00:58:37.009
-All a vampire has is time.
-Not this one.

466
00:58:38.949 --> 00:58:40.178
Right.

467
00:58:40.450 --> 00:58:43.112
The covens are coming for you.

468
00:58:43.286 --> 00:58:47.985
How are you going to spend your last
night. as you always have. alone?

469
00:58:48.158 --> 00:58:49.387
Why not?

470
00:58:50.127 --> 00:58:52.494
Why not share it with me?

471
00:58:56.400 --> 00:58:57.868
All right.

472
00:59:00.604 --> 00:59:04.006
This may be painful for a mortal.

473
00:59:04.207 --> 00:59:07.336
You're still attached to your skin.

474
00:59:08.412 --> 00:59:10.107
I don't care.

475
00:59:12.716 --> 00:59:14.514
Do you trust me?

476
00:59:18.321 --> 00:59:19.811
Yes.

477
00:59:28.965 --> 00:59:31.332
Then close your eyes.

478
01:00:48.745 --> 01:00:50.713
Marius was right.

479
01:00:50.914 --> 01:00:54.077
But I never understood
until I met you.

480
01:00:54.651 --> 01:00:56.676
What do you mean?

481
01:00:56.853 --> 01:01:00.255
You're beautiful to me
because you're human.

482
01:01:00.423 --> 01:01:02.551
Your frailty...

483
01:01:02.826 --> 01:01:04.760
...your short years...

484
01:01:07.197 --> 01:01:08.858
...your heart...

485
01:01:09.065 --> 01:01:11.898
...even as you think it's breaking.

486
01:01:16.273 --> 01:01:18.071
All that...

487
01:01:19.509 --> 01:01:24.174
...seems suddenly more precious
than anything I have ever known.

488
01:01:27.450 --> 01:01:30.283
I'm not as precious as you think.

489
01:01:39.729 --> 01:01:41.163
Do it.

490
01:01:44.734 --> 01:01:46.224
Please.

491
01:01:52.509 --> 01:01:54.739
Let me be with you.

492
01:01:57.047 --> 01:01:59.641
Let me know everything.

493
01:02:07.757 --> 01:02:10.283
You want to know everything?

494
01:02:12.395 --> 01:02:13.988
Come. then.

495
01:02:14.264 --> 01:02:16.062
I'll show you.

496
01:02:38.488 --> 01:02:41.014
What is it? What are we doing--?

497
01:03:26.803 --> 01:03:28.362
Is she all right?

498
01:03:32.709 --> 01:03:35.872
Get away! Get off me!

499
01:03:44.587 --> 01:03:46.214
Now you see?

500
01:03:46.756 --> 01:03:48.190
Are you ready?

501
01:03:49.993 --> 01:03:53.258
Now do you want it. huh?

502
01:03:56.333 --> 01:03:57.459
No.

503
01:03:57.867 --> 01:04:00.564
Of course you don't.

504
01:04:59.863 --> 01:05:02.662
They're pretty worked-up.
How you feeling?

505
01:05:02.832 --> 01:05:04.561
Hey. girls. come on!

506
01:05:05.802 --> 01:05:08.965
Okay. through here. Let him through!

507
01:05:09.406 --> 01:05:10.805
Back off. fella!

508
01:05:11.007 --> 01:05:12.475
Come on. children.

509
01:05:12.675 --> 01:05:14.837
Okay. guys. Come on!

510
01:05:17.180 --> 01:05:19.148
Let him through.

511
01:05:24.721 --> 01:05:26.120
Jesse!

512
01:05:28.725 --> 01:05:30.022
Jesse!

513
01:05:33.897 --> 01:05:35.365
Hello. David.

514
01:05:36.466 --> 01:05:39.800
I must show you my new
paintings sometime.

515
01:08:02.946 --> 01:08:04.141
Find Jesse.

516
01:08:52.595 --> 01:08:54.563
You want more?

517
01:08:58.001 --> 01:09:02.370
This one's for those
who've come for me.

518
01:12:02.185 --> 01:12:03.448
Akasha.

519
01:13:23.099 --> 01:13:25.124
Akasha?!

520
01:13:25.768 --> 01:13:28.328
Why so surprised. my love?

521
01:13:29.105 --> 01:13:31.164
You called. I have come.

522
01:13:32.241 --> 01:13:33.299
My love?

523
01:13:33.809 --> 01:13:36.369
Never fear me. Lestat.

524
01:13:37.446 --> 01:13:39.676
All your wishes have come true.

525
01:13:39.849 --> 01:13:41.510
My wishes?

526
01:13:43.719 --> 01:13:47.280
For a companion to share eternity.

527
01:13:49.825 --> 01:13:53.728
You're bold. like your music.

528
01:13:55.598 --> 01:14:00.536
You live your life in the open.
like I did long ago...

529
01:14:01.704 --> 01:14:03.468
...when I had a king.

530
01:14:03.973 --> 01:14:05.134
Had a king?

531
01:14:05.574 --> 01:14:07.269
He's no more.

532
01:14:08.044 --> 01:14:11.503
Now you are my consort.

533
01:14:12.481 --> 01:14:14.643
That's why I kept you safe.

534
01:14:15.785 --> 01:14:17.310
Alive.

535
01:14:18.321 --> 01:14:19.811
You?

536
01:14:21.557 --> 01:14:24.356
You thought it was all you?

537
01:14:27.496 --> 01:14:30.557
The ego of a king as well.

538
01:14:30.766 --> 01:14:32.256
Yes.

539
01:14:33.536 --> 01:14:36.870
I know you. Lestat.

540
01:14:37.273 --> 01:14:41.335
I know that you crave to have
the world at your feet.

541
01:14:42.845 --> 01:14:46.304
And I have come to give it to you.

542
01:14:48.250 --> 01:14:50.218
Where are we?

543
01:14:51.087 --> 01:14:53.021
<i>We are home.</i>

544
01:14:53.589 --> 01:14:58.823
<i>We live everywhere
and anywhere we choose.</i>

545
01:14:59.228 --> 01:15:02.960
<i>The world is our garden.</i>

546
01:17:27.776 --> 01:17:31.906
<i>All these years I'd hoped
this place was real.</i>

547
01:17:34.083 --> 01:17:39.419
<i>For the first time in my life.
I feel like I'm home.</i>

548
01:17:39.989 --> 01:17:44.051
<i>Strange that this journey
should lead me here.</i>

549
01:17:44.260 --> 01:17:47.491
<i>This place that's haunted my dreams.</i>

550
01:17:52.868 --> 01:17:55.701
<i>Aunt. you're bleeding.</i>

551
01:17:55.905 --> 01:17:58.135
<i>You must be with your own.</i>

552
01:18:00.743 --> 01:18:03.269
<i>I'll always be watching over you.</i>

553
01:18:03.479 --> 01:18:06.210
<i>I want to stay with you forever.</i>

554
01:18:07.416 --> 01:18:09.908
Forever is a very long time.

555
01:18:13.255 --> 01:18:14.882
Aunt Maharet.

556
01:18:24.934 --> 01:18:28.495
You haven't aged.
you haven't changed at all.

557
01:18:31.440 --> 01:18:33.772
I was once a mortal too.

558
01:18:34.109 --> 01:18:38.239
I bore a child before Akasha took me.
I took care of that child...

559
01:18:38.414 --> 01:18:42.078
...and her children.
and her children's children.

560
01:18:42.651 --> 01:18:44.915
This is our family.

561
01:18:45.087 --> 01:18:47.647
My way of coping with eternity.

562
01:18:49.692 --> 01:18:54.528
You are what keeps me connected
to the world of the living.

563
01:18:55.197 --> 01:18:59.327
When your parents died. I brought
you here to take care of you.

564
01:19:04.840 --> 01:19:07.605
Now is not the time.

565
01:19:09.011 --> 01:19:12.777
You were seeking answers
and now you've found them.

566
01:19:13.182 --> 01:19:16.914
The family is who you are.

567
01:20:47.910 --> 01:20:52.074
Drinking my blood allows you
to live in the light.

568
01:20:52.281 --> 01:20:57.219
And soon the sun will no longer
sting your eyes.

569
01:20:58.420 --> 01:21:02.914
This is but a taste
of what we shall share. my love.

570
01:21:04.059 --> 01:21:05.754
My king...

571
01:21:06.595 --> 01:21:09.496
...behold our kingdom.

572
01:21:10.132 --> 01:21:12.499
A kingdom of corpses?

573
01:21:14.503 --> 01:21:17.905
-Why?
-Why not?

574
01:21:18.574 --> 01:21:20.372
This is why you have risen?

575
01:21:20.542 --> 01:21:23.876
They believed in nothing.

576
01:21:24.279 --> 01:21:25.838
Now they are nothing.

577
01:21:32.521 --> 01:21:35.582
But you and I.
we will change all that.

578
01:21:36.792 --> 01:21:41.525
We will give the world something
to believe in again.

579
01:21:42.664 --> 01:21:44.758
Now come. my love.

580
01:21:45.167 --> 01:21:47.226
We have a score to settle.

581
01:21:59.314 --> 01:22:01.976
Since my mortal death.
I have watched...

582
01:22:02.684 --> 01:22:06.985
...I have guided and cared
for my human family...

583
01:22:07.523 --> 01:22:10.424
...generations beyond memory.

584
01:22:12.528 --> 01:22:16.192
This is why we must fight Akasha.

585
01:22:17.533 --> 01:22:22.334
-For the sake of your great family.
-The world we know is about to end.

586
01:22:22.671 --> 01:22:26.665
The only way to prevent this
is through Akasha's destruction.

587
01:22:26.875 --> 01:22:28.365
But how?

588
01:22:28.977 --> 01:22:31.605
When she gives blood.
she's vulnerable.

589
01:22:31.780 --> 01:22:35.648
Whoever takes the last of her blood
will not survive it.

590
01:22:35.851 --> 01:22:37.512
What about Lestat?

591
01:22:37.719 --> 01:22:43.681
Lestat has joined with Akasha.
He's lost to us now. Forget him.

592
01:23:06.381 --> 01:23:07.940
My children.

593
01:23:10.118 --> 01:23:13.213
It warms my blood
to see you all gathered...

594
01:23:13.755 --> 01:23:15.314
...plotting against me.

595
01:23:15.524 --> 01:23:17.959
-Akasha.
-Maharet.

596
01:23:18.760 --> 01:23:23.596
-You will address my king first.
-Lestat. what has she done to you?

597
01:23:26.235 --> 01:23:28.727
Lestat. step aside.

598
01:23:29.238 --> 01:23:30.228
Never.

599
01:23:30.405 --> 01:23:33.067
The world has changed
since you reigned.

600
01:23:33.275 --> 01:23:35.437
Then we shall change it back.

601
01:23:35.777 --> 01:23:37.905
Humans are animals...

602
01:23:38.580 --> 01:23:40.571
...brute creatures.

603
01:23:40.749 --> 01:23:45.983
-Their destruction can only make sense.
-We've found other ways to coexist.

604
01:23:46.188 --> 01:23:50.557
In silence! In shadows and shame!
And for what?

605
01:23:50.726 --> 01:23:52.785
For respect of mortals?

606
01:23:52.961 --> 01:23:55.123
They are nothing to us.

607
01:23:55.297 --> 01:23:57.095
They are merely food.

608
01:23:57.933 --> 01:23:59.367
Akasha. please...

609
01:23:59.568 --> 01:24:02.594
You think you can change my will?

610
01:24:03.238 --> 01:24:06.230
I've had enough of this discussion.

611
01:24:06.408 --> 01:24:08.001
Join me or die.

612
01:24:08.410 --> 01:24:10.105
I will not.

613
01:24:10.312 --> 01:24:12.110
-I will not.
-I will not.

614
01:24:12.314 --> 01:24:13.839
I will not.

615
01:24:22.024 --> 01:24:23.458
Do you love me?

616
01:24:25.360 --> 01:24:28.091
-Yes.
-Then prove it.

617
01:24:30.232 --> 01:24:31.631
Kill her.

618
01:24:32.701 --> 01:24:35.796
-She's nothing to me.
-Just the same...

619
01:24:36.772 --> 01:24:39.173
...I'd like for you to kill her.

620
01:24:43.045 --> 01:24:48.040
-You will not touch her!
-You still think to challenge me?!

621
01:24:51.386 --> 01:24:55.323
-Now.
-No. it's all right. Aunt Maharet.

622
01:24:56.191 --> 01:24:58.125
It's what I want.

623
01:25:04.499 --> 01:25:06.661
How sweet.

624
01:25:12.841 --> 01:25:14.434
I'm ready.

625
01:26:31.219 --> 01:26:33.313
See. my children?

626
01:26:34.489 --> 01:26:37.117
Remember your real family!

627
01:26:38.427 --> 01:26:40.054
Or join hers.

628
01:26:41.329 --> 01:26:42.854
Now...

629
01:26:44.766 --> 01:26:46.632
...give me my crown.

630
01:26:48.303 --> 01:26:50.499
Spoken like a true king.

631
01:26:53.642 --> 01:26:55.269
Come.

632
01:27:05.487 --> 01:27:08.855
You see how he obeys?

633
01:27:09.324 --> 01:27:10.655
You will...

634
01:27:11.660 --> 01:27:14.220
...or you will all die.

635
01:27:19.968 --> 01:27:21.800
That is enough. Lestat.

636
01:27:31.713 --> 01:27:33.647
That is enough. Lestat! Stop!

637
01:28:41.750 --> 01:28:44.276
You kill me...

638
01:28:44.452 --> 01:28:47.478
...you kill yourselves.

639
01:29:32.567 --> 01:29:34.365
Wait. Lestat.

640
01:29:37.138 --> 01:29:38.628
You must stop.

641
01:32:13.595 --> 01:32:16.826
She drank Akasha's last drop.

642
01:32:18.233 --> 01:32:22.101
She took Akasha's death into herself.

643
01:32:23.505 --> 01:32:25.098
She's not dead.

644
01:32:26.074 --> 01:32:28.202
She sleeps.

645
01:33:26.801 --> 01:33:28.326
Hello?

646
01:34:01.136 --> 01:34:02.865
Oh. my God!

647
01:34:03.705 --> 01:34:05.195
Jesse?

648
01:34:06.407 --> 01:34:07.841
Hello. David.

649
01:34:19.521 --> 01:34:21.615
David. this is Lestat.

650
01:34:22.223 --> 01:34:26.251
-Hello.
-I have something for you.

651
01:34:30.098 --> 01:34:31.862
I believe...

652
01:34:32.167 --> 01:34:34.864
...that you wanted this back.

653
01:34:37.005 --> 01:34:40.771
Yes. thank you. Thank you so much.

654
01:34:51.085 --> 01:34:52.951
-Can I ask--?
-What's it like?

655
01:34:54.556 --> 01:34:56.854
Do you want to find out?

656
01:34:57.859 --> 01:34:59.349
Me?

657
01:34:59.527 --> 01:35:02.189
No. I'm too old to live forever.

658
01:35:02.530 --> 01:35:05.397
Well. if you ever change your mind...

659
01:35:08.303 --> 01:35:10.067
So this is goodbye.

660
01:35:11.039 --> 01:35:12.370
Yes.

661
01:36:11.599 --> 01:36:13.590
Hello. David.

661
01:36:14.305 --> 01:37:14.900
